body:
Hi Georgios

Just an FYI on the strange way I'm adding the serializer config. For the life of me I cannot get this to work on reactive nor normal resteasy. The log line is seen but the mapper is not used in either mode. I've always just worked around this by injecting the mapper and adding the config:

```
@Singleton
public class RegisterCustomModuleCustomizer implements ObjectMapperCustomizer {
    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(RegisterCustomModuleCustomizer.class);
    @Override
    public void customize(ObjectMapper jacksonMapper) {
        log.info("Configuring Jackson mapper [{}]", jacksonMapper);
        SimpleModule module = new SimpleModule();
        module.addSerializer(ZonedDateTime.class, new JsonSerializer<ZonedDateTime>() {
            @Override
            public void serialize(ZonedDateTime t, JsonGenerator jg, SerializerProvider sp) throws IOException {
                jg.writeString("aaa");
            }
        });
        jacksonMapper.registerModule(module);
    }
}
```

I completely understand why one would think this looks like a bug, but it's actually not.
It only worked in RESTEasy Classic, sort of by accident.

The proper way to customize an `ObjectMapper` in Quarkus is by using an [ObjectMapperCustomizer](https://quarkus.io/guides/rest-json#jackson).

In your case as you are trying to add a serializer that also added by the `com.fasterxml.jackson.datatype.jsr310.JavaTimeModule`, there is the additional slight complication that you to need to change the priority of the customizer.

Wrapping up, the Quarkus code you need write to make your use case work is:

```java
@Singleton
public class MyCustomizer implements ObjectMapperCustomizer {

    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(RestResource.class);

    @Override
    public int priority() {
        return MINIMUM_PRIORITY; //this is needed in order to ensure that your SimpleModule's Serializer will be applied last and thus override the one coming from the `JavaTimeModule`
    }

    @Override
    public void customize(ObjectMapper objectMapper) {
        log.info("Configuring Jackson mapper [{}]", objectMapper);
        SimpleModule module = new SimpleModule();
        module.addSerializer(ZonedDateTime.class, new JsonSerializer<ZonedDateTime>() {
            @Override
            public void serialize(ZonedDateTime t, JsonGenerator jg, SerializerProvider sp) throws IOException {
                jg.writeString("aaa");
            }

        });
        objectMapper.registerModule(module);
    }
}
```

and then completely drop 

```
@PostConstruct
void init() {
...
}
```

from your Resource.
